==German==

===Alternative forms===
* [[Scheisse]] {{qualifier|Switzerland}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|schize|schīze|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{recons|skītaz|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{recons|skei-d-||to part|lang=ine-pro}}. Indo-European cognates include Ancient Greek {{term|σχιστός|tr=skhistos|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}} and English {{term|shit|lang=en}}, Low Saxon {{term|Schiet|lang=nds}}, Dutch {{term|schijt|land=nl}}, Swedish {{term|skit|lang=sv}} within Germanic.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʃaɪ̯sə/|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|g=f||-}}

# {{vulgar|lang=de}} [[feces]], [[shit]]
#: ''Wo ich hintrete nur '''Scheiße'''!''
# {{vulgar|figuratively|lang=de}} something worthless, [[shit]]
#: ''Das ist doch alles '''Scheiße'''!''

